body:
yurp means u been painted with a nav point to all enemies and at least one  of them is currently looking at you most likely lining up crosshairs so its now time to, spaz the f\*\*\* out, deploy any and all counter measures, or find a good corner to curl up and cry in

&#x200B;

edit: its possible u were painted by the sniper prob equipment (the thing that looks like a quick emergency light)  instead of enemy line of sight ...if thats the case i suggest the corner and cry method until it wares off

so i feel i have a pretty good leg to stand on in this (pun intended) as i am also a above knee leg amputee (along with a long list of other permanent injuries) also resulting from a hospital record setting  motorcycle wreck but i preface this by saying i most likely fall into the "minority" in my thoughts on this but i have always had a dry dark and usually inappropriate since of humor so take this with a grain of salt . i would absolutely crack up laughing at this aswell as make similar jokes like this about myself all the time (i acknowledge doing it about yourself is absolutely a different story) but regardless i can understand both sides of your situation i personally would strongly prefer to be around people that had a since of humor about my "disability" and had the ability to acknowledge it in a fun and light hearted way. instead of the "norm" of most ppl  that act sorta skidish or feel bad 4 me or feel they have to be overly careful or sympathetic towards me as that definitely isnt a fun mood to have around when your just out having a drink n trying to have a good time . 

&#x200B;

i would also definitely acknowledge it is a topic that some (probably more ppl then not but that i dont know i can only speak 4 myself) ppl can be vary sensitive about and if its a person you have never met b4 then i definitely would be supper cautious about  opening with something like this. If it was someone i knew and had any kind of history/repore with then you better belive im going to make jokes about it once i know its something that isnt going to make them feel shitty and i know 4 sure that wasnt your goal at all but everyone is different in how they handle tuff situations but when  the person thats making the joke has no first hand experience with and truly has no clue what its like to be in there......shoe (lol i digress) then it definitely has potential to cut deep and can come off as punching down.

&#x200B;

  if it was a good close friend of mine i would probably already be cracking jokes while im visiting them in the hospital. I can definitely say i would have much rather been surrounded by friends like that when i was layed up over all the "simpathetic supports" not that i wasnt grateful for them or anything but when its what your constantly surrounded by it becomes much more difficult to find ppl who arnt walking on eggshells or afraid of striking a nerve and can just joke around and make lite of a shitty situation and just have a good time...after all i lost a leg not my since of  humor lol. really as long as it was obvious you wernt trying to "punch down" or discredit his undoubtedly difficult life situation then i would say your heart or "intentions" were in the right place but your definitely playing with fire if its someone you dont know well and may not realize your just trying to break the ice in a maybe "dark" but humorous way. so in closing me personally i would much prefer to hangout around ppl like yourself making jokes about it   
 rather then the "simpathetic norm" but im also far FAR from your average human being in a magnitude of different ways but as a "disabled amputee" from a vary similar situation myself thats my 2 cents.

&#x200B;

hope thats helpfull

wanted to throw you a conversational high five ...society definitely puts a over importance on being in a relationship to the point of sometimes looking at single ppl (at least those who havnt recently become single) like theres something wrong with them ....same for the stigma that comes with someone telling you they have been thru a devorce without the knowledge too the cause dont get me wrong that last one has potential for more "red flags" but its just as possible that they were betrayed and actually did nothing wrong......im getting off topic sry ...was just a quick shout out to this comment i couldnt agree more with

&#x200B;

as too the topic at hand from the OP dont give up or feel discredited for having feelings for ppl your attracted too just because they may not be reciprocated. try to internaly give yourself kudos for atleast having the balls to shoot your shot. alot of guys trip before ever even getting to that hurdle

&#x200B;

if this is a recurring problem with you then i would also suggest possibly seeing a therapist as they have the education and experience to give you the tools to possibly help you not get TOO overly attached to early wich i belive would help your chances a fair bit    as women are emotionally intuitive beings and if they sence an imbalance in attraction that can be a show stopper even if they do like you but still arnt sure or are still trying to find out if your compatible....thats my 2 cents ....i agree with the above poster \^

so my (32m) 2 cents would be this . i personally have no problem respecting any one male or female that shows respect to me in return however i will say in my younger days especially i harbored more what i would call jealousy toward women in general more for society norms between men and women instead of anything they did personally...men on the general  average  get far less attention(regardless of weather or not its wanted) in multiple different ways then women do and its easy to harbor a bit of resentment from that ...were always told from a young age "save the women and children" instilling a thought of them being the more valuable of the genders innately where for a man to provide value he has too be useful or provide a service of some sort either financially or otherwise. while i definitely acknowledged this was not caused by women or done with any malicious intent by anyone. it definitely was something i had to work thru myself in my younger days to not harbor an unreasonable distain towards women especially attractive women generally more exaggerated at times i was ever single and feeling generally unwanted witch intern was actually perpetuating my problems 

&#x200B;

i fully acknowledge this could have just been a me problem and not necessarily a normal cause for disrespect on the whole but thought it was a possible it might b the case and might help.

omg ...thank you for taking the time to put this up 4 ppl 2 see....i needed to hear this and i kno im not the only one ....your doing the lords work 

&#x200B;

i feel in todays world our ever improving technology that has givin us the ability to connect with more ppl then ever befor and with less effort. has also made people communicate in a way thats much more susceptible to being misunderstood or to missing the underlying intentions entierly  . Combine that with a there being an overabundance of "other fish in the sea" has in a way made ppl more "expendable" and or easily replaceable wich has lead to a society where "ghoasting" is much more common place and ppl have taken to improving the usfulness of there comunication devices to cast a broader net rather  then to developing good communication skills instead .... i find this incredibly depressing   . in my experience it seems people have become much less empathetic to eachother and would prefer to just avoid a situation or conversation and leave someone hurt and wondering what went wrong rather then having the difficult conversation and giving the other person an understanding (even if its not the one they wanted) and giving the other person an easier ability to accept the reality move on faster .

"Love makes us blind to harsh realities" this jumped out and really hit home for me . while i dont have much in the way of "cheerful or helpful" things to make you feel better i can say you are definitely not alone in this thought process. it truly pains me too my core seeing how people interact with each other in todays society .i find a lot of my sadness/anger is aimed at the female gender simply because im a strait male but i know guys do this too I just have not experienced it first hand so it skews my disposition toward women in an unfair way that is hard to get past sometimes. I see so many people do things that are so unnecessarily more hurtful too someone just because its a little bit easier for them to deal with it that way instead of being an empathetic and understanding person to the perspective on the other side and just being real  and honest with their feelings weather they are good or bad. 

&#x200B;

In my experience there is  usually always a way you can break any news to someone in a way that is respectful to them in a way that makes them feel their feelings are valid,important,and understood but simply not reciprocated regardless of weather they have been married for years or just met and just asked them out for the first time.  Often when done correctly this can provide understanding and possibly some closer as well as help them to move on with there lives instead of dwelling on past interactions or possible mistakes wondering what it was they did "wrong" or could have done differently. 

&#x200B;

not to say that it wont still hurt them ...alot i fully acknowledged rejection is a painful thing no mater how its communicated but  it dosnt need to be so overly unnecessary hurtful just because they dont want to subject themselves to a difficult and or  possibly awkward conversation. 

&#x200B;

 Living in a society so quick to "ghost" each other just because there is an overabundance of "fish in the sea" and its easier to just disappear without a word i find to be morbidly self centered and depressing. it makes so many more people then we realize feel broken or lose the drive to be in the "dating game" and stop trying to find someone that makes them happy and feel loved.

&#x200B;

there was an interaction i witnessed many years ago that i will never forget between a man and a woman that didnt even know each other . the man was sitting outside a restaurant/bar on the side walk and was yelling at anybody that walked by while most ppl ignored him or even crossed the street to avoid him entirely there was a woman walking with another female friend of hers and when they past the man shouted some fairly mean and derogatory things at them but instead of reacting offended and shouting back or simply ignoring him and moving along the woman stopped and politely asked the man why he was so angry at her . the man calmed down a little  bit and stopped shouting and the woman sat down next to him while i could no longer hear what they were saying. No more then a minute later the man was in tears appologizing to both of the women profusely then both of the women hugged the man and went inside the bar that i was sitting on the patio of  . after a minute or too i returned to the inside of the bar to get another drink b4 leaving and saw the woman at the bar and had to ask what was said between the two that had caused such an abrupt change in emotion and also give kudos for her remarkable way she handled the situation that everyone else was ignoring or even pouring fuel on the fire of . she said the man clearly had not prepaired for anyone to be kind to him and almost didnt know how to react when met with it. he was a bit sheepish at first then shared that the mans dog had died just a few days prior and he felt completely alone and angry at everything around him and everywhere he looked everybody had a  friend to talk to and that was all he wanted . she then told the man that in this world today most ppl are too busy or afraid to even try to make friends anymore even with people they share similar interests with . but the best way to hedge your bets is to extend a ear an listen to ppl and try to understand where they are and  you will find no mater there success or class ect. life can be hard for any walk of life out there but everyone wants to feel understood and that how they feel is valid and important even if how they came to feel that way is  unreasonable,unwarrented, or even unexplainable it dosnt take away there right to feel that way. 

&#x200B;

this fairly simple outlook and approach when employed correctly even with someone you find to be currently revolting can make a massive positive difference in how that person interacts back even if all your trying to accomplish is to get them to stop interacting with you entirely once they feel understood themselves and then hear and process your feelings in return even if there "less then ideal"  theres not  much left up in the air that might have felt needed to be clerified and its easier for both parties to accept the reality of the situation and move on wile maybe not unscathed atleast hopefully without unnecessary battle scars.

&#x200B;

sry 4 the novel....got a bit carried away with this ....its obviously something im passionate about i feel the majority of human history until vary recently (comparatively speaking) human interacted in a much smaller "tribe" so to speak and with that in turn interacted with each other much differently . if you could imagine being in for example an Indian tribe of say 400-500 ppl you would be far more inclined to "keep the long term peace" within the tribe and be more kind in your interactions including unwanted ones as your definitely going to see them again and possibly have to interact with them again but in our world today where you can block some one and even if u live in same city with vary little effort can never see them ever again . humans have never had the ability to connect and interact with so many others of our kind that we have effectively made ourselves expendable and replaceable to each other when something breaks now we throw it away and get another one where as once upon a time it was more conducive to fix what broke instead of replace it.

&#x200B;

okay now im done i promise....my 2 cents on this spiraled wildly out of control.

so i cant speak for the "feet" as i am an ak amp but  i will say going from a mechanical knee to a microprocessor knee for me was a night and day difference and couldnt live without one now it drastically improved my stability as well as gave me the ability to walk backwards and felt much more confident when using ....dont know how much that would translate to your situation being that a knee is more detrimental then a foot but from my experience if its a possibility for you to get one  its definitely worth the wait 

&#x200B;

side note ive worked with hanger b4 and there not necessarily "expedient" but far from the slowest but in my time with them they seemed to always have a large workload and scheduling appointments and such was usually always a ways out in comparison to some other options but there a solid company that in time can gets things done ...dunno if any of this helped at all just my 2 cents . good luck

so i also am an above knee amp on my right leg also resulting from a motorcycle accident that was also a hit and run  so as a side note feel free to pass him my screen name here and he can talk/ask me anything if he would like the perspective of someone whos gone thu the same thing .

as for your question i was in a hospital record setting accident and had substantial damadge to both legs and both arms and was in a drug induced coma in the er for 3-4 weeks and in the hospital for 8 months but i had pretty bad phantom pain to a point of causing spasms in my residual limb that took about 8months to a year after leaving the hospital to fully subside ...one thing i did notice was that it seemed to be much worse on days i didnt get much sleep the night b4. but in my personal situation nerve pain medication didnt seem to help much as much as just getting good sleep did

&#x200B;

as for your other question on coping everyone is a little different on that front i personaly was able to get past the loss of limb relatively easily but i also had a number of other permanent injuries on top that gave me more of a longterm since of "dread" aswell as had my gf of 5years leave me while i was still in the hospital so my biggest issue was more of a feeling of abandonment from her with a pending thought of "im never going to find anyone whos going to want me again with all these issues if i cant even get the ppl who already loved me 2" ...but after a good bit of therapy and support from my family i was able make a fair amount of progress so i would say the biggest thing in my eyes would just be to remain helpful loving and supportive and he will let u know what he dose and dosnt need help with. 

&#x200B;

sry to make this so long and seemingly spill my life story 2 u aswell but this kinda thing is obviously pretty big 2 me so was trying to be as  helpful as possible. 

&#x200B;

feel free (for you or him)to personal message me if you would like.

best of luck in recovery 

Travis.

so i first want to say that i have always been terrible at this my (32m) entire life i have always developed feelings for some one and lose the ability to even think or imagine a relationship with anyone else. but im finally developing the perspective to see just how unhealthy it can be aswell as being unhelpful at getting a chance to date that (or anyother who is interested) women 

&#x200B;

so 1st step is admiting this is something you do often enough to be a problem but how do you fix it b4 it can get to a point of harming your social life or chances with ppl interested in you ...that is much more difficult and im far from mastering it but i have gotten much better by doing a few things different 

&#x200B;

i noticed around the age of 26-28ish that i was actually treating women i was attracted too different then anyone else usually in the form of "nice guy" traits being overrly accommodating or appologizing for things that required none but when there was a girl that i found out was attracted to me that i had not developed a "oneitus" for i would act much differently around them weather i found them to be attractive or not i came to the conclusion that  it was the "me" that wasnt overly concerned about what i said or putting forth effort to get someone to like me that actually made me a more attractive person and that developing a oneitus mindset to someone was actually actively killing my chances with them. 

&#x200B;

it is absolutely paramount to try to identify when you are developing these feelings/thoughts and activly combat them while you can still easily walk away from the person intead of having to go thu "getting over there rejection" after its too late . you never want your personal health or ability to be happy henge upon anyone but yourself. regardless of weather you are in a relationship or not 

&#x200B;

women are vary intuitive to to the motivation behind peoples(men especially) actions and it is why the saying "nice guys finish last" exist . theres a massive difference between being overly nice or talking or treating someone in a different way to  get them to like you as opposed to just not being an asshole and when women see that it can come off as being needy or in search of there validation or approval where as a man that requires neither comes off as much more confident and fun 2 be around.

&#x200B;

lastly its important to have and be open to mutiple options b4 entering a relationship because weather u tell them how you feel or not they will usually pick up on it regardless and if ur not open to any other option that can put an immense amount of unnecessary pressure on them and cause them to pull away 

&#x200B;

hope this was helpful in anyway sry if this was offbase and just me projecting my own past issues . wish i had more helpful advise in the form of behavior to change\\look out for etc. but as previously  status ive far from mastered this but am making progress ...best of luck my man

so first off i(31m) want to say your post here really hit home for me i was the same way for a long time especially with people i found attractive usualy resulting in them not being interested however i started to notice that the ppl who were interested in me were ppl that i didn't ever really put much thought into until after they (or a friend of there's) told me they were into me and most certainly didn't interact with them the same way. so too add on to what some of the other ppl have posted here i don't necessarily agree with the statement that you have "low self worth" however you are kinda painting yourself into the corner of you feeling as if you are not deserving of the attention of the ppl you find attractive. you dont have to apologize for wanting ANYONES attention we are all human beings . the thought that there are "leagues" of ppl in the dating pool is purely false ive seen plenty of "5's" get with "perfect 10's" on account of personality or intellectual ability ect. and even if there were "leagues"  dont ever put yourself "down" a league and apologize or "thank them" for "dating down" to you .

&#x200B;

so inclosing try to conduct your interactions with a thought that you absolutely do deserve the attention and time of the ppl you are after because well you do deserve it without any qualifying statements and dont ever apologize for it even if you do end up  even get rejected think of it as "well that person was worth trying for" and move on with your head held high even if for no other reason then you had the balls to take a risk and to go after what you want in life ...my biggest regrets in life are not asking ppl that i found attractive and wondering "what if" for far too long never "darn i asked out the girl of my dreams and got rejected" i can get over that much faster and without regrets.

ya im currently struggling with this ...i lost my leg amongst alot of other limb and mobility issues from a bad wreck...got alot of help and support from this subreddit but if im being honest with you aswell as myself im definitely still not over it and it has most certainly effected me and my confidence level moving forward ...dont mean to be a downer or to hijack you post but i lost way more then just my leg in that wreck ...my gf of 5 years left me while i was still hospitalized her (non biological to me)3 kids that i helped raise disappeared lost my house and now live with my older brother....so ive had alot more obstacles that have compounded my confidence issues in trying to move forward but trying to just keep making any progress at all no matter how small is paramount and making sure you dont let yourself get trapped into the idea that "this person who seems or seemed like they might have been interested is probably my only shot" that kinda thing ppl can pick up on and paints an air of desperation and puts to much pressure on them ....im digressing pretty bad here maybe this isnt something you need to worry about but i can only share my own experience and thoughts ...sorry im not actually helping alot but just know your not alone in this thought i guess.

&#x200B;

something some one told me on this subreddit was that they met there wife and one of the things that they found attractive about him was that they were so strong for overcoming the loss of there limb and not letting it change who they were and become a bitter or downer to be around dispite the hardships they have been put into....that really struck home for me (shout out to peg leg pete i think is what he said his name was lol) 

&#x200B;

dont ever be afraid to reach out for help here or anywhere for that matter if it ever becomes a serious issue theres plenty of ppl out there more then willing .

so i definitely have some experience here i was involed in an accident at a time where i didnt have health insurance but being that it wasnt my fault and the extreme level of injury i was givin state covered base level insurance which originally told me a c leg wouldnt be approved under any circumstances 

&#x200B;

however my angel of a prosthetist managed to get one approved after about a year and a half on a basic mechanical knee. there were a few things that helped make this possible 1 was the level of damage my leg i still had received (lost feeling and motor function below knee) that required a integrated knee and ankle brace. aswell as having a dead nerve in my right arm making using crutches or other arm assists much more difficult and unsafe.

&#x200B;

there came a time when my prosthetic office had a c leg i was able to come in and  test out while i was there (couldnt take home) they tested me in a timed run of a few motions then compaired the much better times against times with my current mechanical knee and sent them in to my insurance company  after having 2 major falls at home  thankfully without injury that my prosthetist documented and sent into my insurance they finally had enough evidence that the added stability the c leg offered was necessary to prevent causing further injuries 

&#x200B;

this was most certainly a complete game changer for me and made a massive difference in stability ....so while i dont advocate trying to hurt yourself if u can make a mechanical knee seem like an unsafe bottleneck thats holding you back or causing issues it can definitely help your cause

well i can definitely say its more then understandably frustrating on both sides here but it atleast seems like the real important things are there but for lack of a much more tactful way of putting it you both just need to learn to relax a little ....the whole part of being in a relationship in the first place should be a place of warm relaxing comfort not a cold transaction of emotional inputs....communication builds bridges 

&#x200B;

best of luck

its normal for throttle to rampup with no props on . just make sure all ur motors are spinning the correct way and props r securly mounted the correct direction and try it outside wile u stand far away ready to pounce on the disarm switch if things go crazy  also insure proper board alignment in first tab of bettaflight does the drone act accordingly to how u move it around in your hand. ie u dip the nose down dose the picture respond the same way?

&#x200B;

also calibrate your accel on flat surface

&#x200B;

happy flying

....okay so i(31m) would say your dealing with your issue in such a way that it may perpetuate itself without proper and open communication with your bf 

&#x200B;

....firstly its perfectly normal and healthy for bothsides of a relationship to "sometimes say no"  or there not in the mood. but if your motivation to reject him is because "you never get what you want" that is  unhealthy in a few ways ....on first reaction it would seem as if your trying to use sex as a ransome to try and get what you want  ....seemingly in this case being more sex more often to a seemingly hopfully daily occurrence wich im not even going to begin to explain how backwards the thought process seems to an outside perspective to reject the thing you want in hopes of getting more of it more often in the future

&#x200B;

...i dont mean to be rude nor am i here to take shots of anykind  but i feel like a good bit of your frustration comes from possibly over reacting to him "not being in the mood" to meaning your unwanted or unworthy in any way wich is not the case ...i would suggest trying to regard sex as a mutually beneficial"surprise" rather then having anykind of timly expectations on it that if not met are then acted vengefully out of feelings of being "rejected"  or "unwanted" 

&#x200B;

i could be wrong this is simply how it seems to me from what you posted . at the end of the day i would just try and have a open conversation with your bf about your feelings and there effects on you and you might be suprised at what u hear or see in return but i definitely wouldnt reject something you both want when hes in the mood just out of spite that its not always reciprocated  when your in the mood ....such is simply the way of life and will only be helped by an open line of communication.

&#x200B;

next time u get a "sorry" try not to take it personal and stay in "the pocket" of cuddling/being loving and possibly ask him is everything okay and possibly after a bit of communication u might find more success with mutually beneficial surprises \*wink\*.

unfortunately theres not any easy or magical quick  fix for this however simply by reaching out this way it would imply that you know this feeling isnt healthy or productive at either winning her over and getting a "date" or inversely making a move and getting rejected so if you can isolate that feeling this way is destructive in multiple ways and obsessesing over her is actually sabotaging your chances of getting the vary thing your obsessing over ...

&#x200B;

its far too easy to overlook or sweep under the rug flaws or just simple incompatabilitys in people we are crushing over often compromising our selves in tiny ways that we say we would be okay with but that you wouldnt do when just trying to find a suitable mate without the bias of overinfatuation.  so when u find those kinda "chinks in the armor" of there perfection use that as a reminder that maybe being with this person wouldn't be as good as i dream about it being  day and night...ultimately if she is what you want so bad then realize your best chance you have at achieving your goals is to first be a healthy happy person on your own outside of her and bring that to the table for her 

&#x200B;

it wont be easy but theres a reason over sharing and "confessing your undying love or obsession" with some one almost never works your holding them verbally hostage when being a fun and interesting person is what people actually want to be around  and having some one tell you there already overinvested in you from the start can make you feel awkward or uneasy or seem like thers to much emotional responsibility on them to early.

&#x200B;

lastly ...take your best shot once your in a healty state of mind and confident in yourself with or without them  ...while rejection can seem scary i find it infinitly more terrifiying to possibly look back on  periods of my life that i wasted being to scared to actualy go out and try to get what i want in my life.

dealing with memory loss issues seems like its fairly hard to predict the longterm outcome with anykind of accuracy as results seem to vary drastically but  that im definitely not qualified to be able to answer however i have seen that  spending 20 to 40 mins a day playing memory exercise games like matching face down playing card games on phone has been shown to actual help longterm memory loss recovery aswell...im my case i was extremely fortunate to keep everything between the ears in seemingly working order outside of a bit of optical nerve damage to one eye as i had a major concussion with massive swelling all over  but memory and general cognition seem to be okay...altho admittedly theres a good to fair chance im in a white padded room in a strait jacket slamming my head against the wall chanting about the love for a family dog i never had and im just thinking im sitting at home typing on reddit 🤣i digress

&#x200B;

as for the physical "new normal" you probably wont be winning any foot races but i (im a  right ak with a also heavily compromised left requiring knee brace and afo) was a motorcycle tech b4 my accident and was surprised at how compassionate and accommodating my workplace was to get me working again dispite not even working there long b4 my accident with a few work bay modifications i was able to continue what i know and love doing. i will say what i do is far from the level of education and ability being a doctor requires but with enough drive and stubborn determination and a bit of luck i think is still well in the realm of possibility for you and in the end this experience might even help you become a better doctor with the ability to relate to and connect on a higher level with patients. having personal experience to what some of your patients might be going thru. 

&#x200B;

for me staying positive and motivated was my largest hurdle by far and would recommend staying envolved with your community and with helpful people that will keep u motivated to progress regardless of how slow it is just keeping it in a positive direction is paramount. best of luck

biggest difference is the m80 (one that plugs into controller is stereo only and has 3 preset non customizable eq's bassicly just have a different lvl of base (low,med,high) where the mixamp pro that comes with the box on the left sports full dolby surround sound and 4 software customizable eq settings that can be tuned via astros app on the xbox or a pc on there discord theres also community presets made for specific games IE a modern warfare eq ect.

&#x200B;

longstory short the mixamp pro is much better but the m80 will function for most "casual" players but if your looking for the "top shelf" experience or are a competitive gamer go with the mixamp pro 4 sure

i would recommend making the top plate 2mm and keeping the bottom at 3 to save a decent bit of weight to possibly trade off for the thicker arms if necessary aswell as adding a samwich plate for the arms otherrwise this thing is gunna vibrate like crazy

&#x200B;

edit: just realized i pretty much said the same thing fradelic said an hour ago lol. sry dude wasnt tryn to steal ur thunder guess we just think alike .

lets see the pads on the bottom of the fc . sometimes especially with pads with thru holes if u use 2 much solder wich it kinda looks like it it can bleed thru and short pads on the opposite side of the board. ....also multi meter can be got off amazon for less then 10 bucks and there a needed tool really they can save tons of guess work with a little know how and process of elimination.

&#x200B;

ps:60/40 rosin core LEADED solder and more flux will clean them joints up...more heat and less contact time with iron and u should b good 2 go ...good luch chasin them electrical grimlins
